architecture-audit/cycle-010-backend-frontend-project-contract/reviews/round-01-review.md:29:Both proposals correctly identify the core architectural reality from the scope check: the active project persistence boundary is frontend command-stream `ProjectData` via `ProjectPersistencePort` and Drive/app-shell flows, while the backend `/api/projects` stack is a disconnected stale DTO path and `OpenProjectDialog.vue` is a dead frontend surface with a direct backend implementation import (`scope-check.md`; `frontend/src/services/ProjectService.ts`; `frontend/src/application/appShell/ProjectSessionUseCases.ts`; `frontend/src/components/dialogs/OpenProjectDialog.vue`; `backend/src/models/Project.ts`; `backend/src/api/projects.ts`).
architecture-audit/cycle-010-backend-frontend-project-contract/reviews/round-01-review.md:33:However, both proposals miss one required in-place correction before decision: they do not explicitly delete or replace the still-present frontend e2e spec that targets the stale backend `/api/projects` contract. That leaves behind a direct test artifact for the disconnected backend path they are proposing to remove, which conflicts with the wave's aggressive-deletion priority and would create immediate validation/doc drift after implementation.
architecture-audit/cycle-010-backend-frontend-project-contract/reviews/round-01-review.md:45:| 5. Introduced risks/hidden regressions | 3/5 | Main hidden risk is incomplete cleanup: obsolete frontend e2e spec still targets `/api/projects`; backend-workspace retention criteria are slightly under-specified. |
architecture-audit/cycle-010-backend-frontend-project-contract/reviews/round-01-review.md:58:| 5. Introduced risks/hidden regressions | 3/5 | Same hidden cleanup gap: obsolete frontend e2e spec for `/api/projects` is not named in files-to-change/delete list. |
architecture-audit/cycle-010-backend-frontend-project-contract/reviews/round-01-review.md:65:1. **Explicitly handle obsolete frontend e2e persistence spec.** Both proposals must add `frontend/tests/e2e/persistence.spec.ts` to the delete-or-replace list, because it still targets `localhost:3000/api/projects` and stale backend DTO behavior rather than the active app-shell/Drive `ProjectData` flow. This artifact was already identified as obsolete in Wave 004 review history and remains present now. Leaving it unnamed would preserve a disconnected stale backend test path after this wave.
architecture-audit/cycle-010-backend-frontend-project-contract/reviews/round-01-review.md:66:2. **Tie validation plan to that deletion/replacement.** The corrected proposal should state that e2e/Playwright validation for Wave 010 must cover the active startup/open project flow and must not rely on the deleted backend `/api/projects` test path.
architecture-audit/cycle-010-backend-frontend-project-contract/reviews/round-01-review.md:70:- **Delete-backend stance:** justified by current code evidence. The frontend active path uses `ProjectService` command-stream persistence and Drive/app-shell flows, not backend HTTP (`frontend/src/services/ProjectService.ts`; `frontend/src/application/appShell/ProjectSessionUseCases.ts`). The only frontend/backend coupling found is the dead `OpenProjectDialog.vue` type import from backend implementation source. The backend DTO/API is therefore stale and disconnected.
architecture-audit/cycle-010-backend-frontend-project-contract/reviews/round-01-review.md:72:- **Disconnected stale backend preservation:** not acceptable. Any decision that keeps the current `ProjectDTO` + `/api/projects` path without converting it to the active command-stream contract would fail the wave objective.
architecture-audit/cycle-010-backend-frontend-project-contract/reviews/round-01-review.md:82:- Confirmed backend mounts `/api/projects` in `backend/src/server.ts`.
architecture-audit/cycle-010-backend-frontend-project-contract/reviews/round-01-review.md:83:- Confirmed backend `ProjectDTO` is broad and stale relative to frontend `ProjectData`.
architecture-audit/cycle-010-backend-frontend-project-contract/reviews/round-01-review.md:84:- Confirmed `OpenProjectDialog.vue` imports `ProjectMetadata` from `backend/src/models/Project` and calls nonexistent `projectService.listProjects()` / `loadProject()` methods, reinforcing that it is dead/stale.
architecture-audit/cycle-010-backend-frontend-project-contract/reviews/round-01-review.md:87:- Confirmed repo still contains `frontend/tests/e2e/persistence.spec.ts` targeting stale backend `/api/projects`, so proposals must explicitly clean it up.
architecture-audit/cycle-010-backend-frontend-project-contract/scope-check.md:11:The core premise still holds after Wave 009: the repository contains a backend Express/file-storage project API with its own broad `any` project DTO shape, while the active frontend project lifecycle uses the Wave 004 command-stream `ProjectService` through the Wave 009 app-shell runtime and Google Drive ports. The only frontend/backend coupling found in active source is not a real API boundary; it is a direct TypeScript import from `frontend/src/components/dialogs/OpenProjectDialog.vue` into `backend/src/models/Project.ts`. The active app shell no longer renders that dialog, so the import leak is also attached to a dead/obsolete frontend component rather than a validated backend integration.
architecture-audit/cycle-010-backend-frontend-project-contract/scope-check.md:13:Recommended stance for proposals: prefer deleting the unused backend project API and the dead `OpenProjectDialog.vue` surface. A keep-backend alternative is still viable for review, but it must make the backend a real typed project boundary and add backend/root validation; it should not preserve the current disconnected backend plus frontend implementation import leak.
architecture-audit/cycle-010-backend-frontend-project-contract/scope-check.md:29:`backend/src/models/Project.ts` defines `ProjectDTO` with separate `elements2D`, `elements3D`, `dependencyGraph`, `planes`, `hingeLines`, `view2D`, `processTree`, and optional `commandHistory` fields (`backend/src/models/Project.ts:6-52`). Several central fields are `Array<any>` or `any` (`backend/src/models/Project.ts:13-14`, `backend/src/models/Project.ts:43`, `backend/src/models/Project.ts:50`). This does not match the active Wave 004 frontend contract, where `ProjectData` contains `schemaVersion`, `nextElementId`, and committed command snapshots (`frontend/src/services/ProjectService.ts:11-19`) and is validated as schema version `6.0.0` (`frontend/src/services/ProjectService.ts:24-31`, `frontend/src/services/ProjectService.ts:80-129`).
architecture-audit/cycle-010-backend-frontend-project-contract/scope-check.md:31:`createEmptyProject()` creates backend-only default state with `P_H`, `P_V`, `HL_HV`, empty element arrays, empty dependency graph, and process root (`backend/src/models/Project.ts:67-120`). The active frontend initializes its world through `initializeWorld()` inside app-shell session flows instead (`frontend/src/application/appShell/ProjectSessionUseCases.ts:27-32`, `frontend/src/application/appShell/ProjectSessionUseCases.ts:96-110`).
architecture-audit/cycle-010-backend-frontend-project-contract/scope-check.md:35:`backend/src/server.ts` mounts `projectsRouter` at `/api/projects` (`backend/src/server.ts:1-15`). `backend/src/api/projects.ts` exposes list/create/get/update/delete route handlers (`backend/src/api/projects.ts:11-110`) backed by `ProjectRepository` (`backend/src/api/projects.ts:1-5`). Update accepts the request body as `updates` with no DTO validation beyond existence (`backend/src/api/projects.ts:65-77`). Error handlers use `error: any` (`backend/src/api/projects.ts:15-18`, `backend/src/api/projects.ts:35-38`, `backend/src/api/projects.ts:55-58`, `backend/src/api/projects.ts:78-84`, `backend/src/api/projects.ts:103-108`).
architecture-audit/cycle-010-backend-frontend-project-contract/scope-check.md:39:`FileStorage.readJSON<T>()` parses arbitrary file JSON directly to `T` (`backend/src/storage/FileStorage.ts:28-38`) and `writeJSON<T>()` serializes arbitrary data (`backend/src/storage/FileStorage.ts:44-52`). `ProjectRepository.list()` trusts files as `ProjectDTO` and extracts metadata, logging and skipping unreadable files (`backend/src/storage/ProjectRepository.ts:27-47`). `ProjectRepository.update()` merges `Partial<ProjectDTO>` into an existing project and rewrites `updatedAt`, preserving id/createdAt (`backend/src/storage/ProjectRepository.ts:78-95`). This is a backend persistence path, but it is neither the frontend command-stream contract nor a validated shared contract.
architecture-audit/cycle-010-backend-frontend-project-contract/scope-check.md:43:`backend/tests/integration/projects.spec.ts` tests `/api/projects` creation, loading, update, list, sort, and delete behavior (`backend/tests/integration/projects.spec.ts:39-342`). The tests assert backend DTO defaults such as `planes`, `hingeLines`, `elements2D`, `elements3D`, `dependencyGraph`, `processTree`, and `view2D` (`backend/tests/integration/projects.spec.ts:51-81`, `backend/tests/integration/projects.spec.ts:135-154`, `backend/tests/integration/projects.spec.ts:171-215`). They do not exercise frontend `ProjectService` command streams or the app-shell Drive flow.
architecture-audit/cycle-010-backend-frontend-project-contract/scope-check.md:47:`frontend/src/components/dialogs/OpenProjectDialog.vue` imports the runtime `projectService` and imports `ProjectMetadata` by reaching across the monorepo into backend implementation source: `import type { ProjectMetadata } from '../../../../backend/src/models/Project';` (`frontend/src/components/dialogs/OpenProjectDialog.vue:54-58`). It stores `projects` as `ProjectMetadata[]` (`frontend/src/components/dialogs/OpenProjectDialog.vue:68`) and calls `projectService.listProjects()` / `projectService.loadProject()` (`frontend/src/components/dialogs/OpenProjectDialog.vue:83-108`). Those methods do not exist on the current `frontend/src/services/ProjectService.ts`, which only exposes static command-stream serialization, validation, and deserialization (`frontend/src/services/ProjectService.ts:24-133`).
architecture-audit/cycle-010-backend-frontend-project-contract/scope-check.md:49:Search found no active source import of the component by component name; current app-shell UI renders `StartupDialog`, not `OpenProjectDialog` (`frontend/src/App.vue:1-16`, `frontend/src/App.vue:91-108`). Toolbar open-project emits to `runtime.actions.openProjectDialog` (`frontend/src/App.vue:26-32`), which only sets the StartupDialog visible (`frontend/src/application/appShell/AppShellRuntime.ts:137-145`, `frontend/src/application/appShell/ProjectSessionUseCases.ts:150-152`). Therefore the direct backend import leak is real in the source tree but appears attached to a dead dialog surface.
architecture-audit/cycle-010-backend-frontend-project-contract/scope-check.md:67:This is consistent with Wave 004’s current-format-only command/undo persistence direction and inconsistent with backend `ProjectDTO`.
architecture-audit/cycle-010-backend-frontend-project-contract/proposals/proposal-restructure.md:5:This proposal evaluates whether the right fix sits one conceptual layer higher than deleting files: the architecture needs a single project persistence contract owned by application/shared contract code, with concrete storage adapters behind it. On inspection, the current code already has a strong frontend-side application contract from Wave 004 and Wave 009: command-stream `ProjectData` plus `ProjectPersistencePort`. The backend’s `ProjectDTO` is not a storage adapter for that contract; it is a competing project model.
architecture-audit/cycle-010-backend-frontend-project-contract/proposals/proposal-restructure.md:21:- **The backend is not an adapter for that boundary.** It exposes `/api/projects` over a separate `ProjectDTO` shape (`backend/src/models/Project.ts:6-52`) and unvalidated file repository (`backend/src/storage/ProjectRepository.ts:27-95`).
architecture-audit/cycle-010-backend-frontend-project-contract/proposals/proposal-restructure.md:22:- **The frontend import leak is not a valid shared contract.** `OpenProjectDialog.vue` imports `ProjectMetadata` from backend implementation source (`frontend/src/components/dialogs/OpenProjectDialog.vue:54-58`) but the component appears unused by current `App.vue`, which renders `StartupDialog` (`frontend/src/App.vue:1-16`, `frontend/src/App.vue:91-108`).
architecture-audit/cycle-010-backend-frontend-project-contract/proposals/proposal-restructure.md:29:- A focused architecture test forbids frontend imports from `backend/src/**`.
architecture-audit/cycle-010-backend-frontend-project-contract/proposals/proposal-restructure.md:31:- Obsolete e2e coverage for `localhost:3000/api/projects` is deleted or replaced with coverage of active app-shell/startup/open-project/project-persistence behavior.
architecture-audit/cycle-010-backend-frontend-project-contract/proposals/proposal-restructure.md:37:- Create a shared contract module/package, for example `shared/project-contract` or `specs/contracts` generated types, containing `ProjectData`, `SerializedCommand`, operation descriptor union references, `ProjectMetadata`, and runtime validators.
architecture-audit/cycle-010-backend-frontend-project-contract/proposals/proposal-restructure.md:39:- Change backend models from `ProjectDTO` to the shared command-stream `ProjectData` contract, deleting `elements2D`, `elements3D`, `dependencyGraph`, `planes`, `hingeLines`, `view2D`, `processTree`, and `commandHistory` as standalone backend DTO fields.
architecture-audit/cycle-010-backend-frontend-project-contract/proposals/proposal-restructure.md:44:This would satisfy Wave 010 only if the backend becomes a real active boundary. It is not recommended for this wave because current app behavior is Drive-based, no frontend source fetches `/api/projects`, and adding a second storage adapter now would broaden scope toward product feature work rather than architectural deletion.
architecture-audit/cycle-010-backend-frontend-project-contract/proposals/proposal-restructure.md:52:- `frontend/tests/unit/application/appShell/AppShellBoundary.test.ts` or a new focused architecture spec: add/adjust assertions that no frontend source imports from `backend/src` and no active component imports `OpenProjectDialog`.
